iners' layers'","observability.sh:521 uses only `docker system df --format '{{.Type}}|{{.Size}}'` — `.Reclaimable` is not currently used in-repo (Partially-verified: command used, this field surface unconfirmed)","docker system df `--format` supports Go-template fields but the exact field set (`.Reclaimable`) and its meaning per row is unverified from this environment"],"finding":"The plan asserts a NEW `docker system df` format-field surface — `{{.Reclaimable}}` — and a specific semantic mapping (Containers-row `.Size` = all writable layers; `.Reclaimable` = stopped containers' layers) that the repo's existing `docker_ledger_bytes` does not exercise (it reads only `{{.Type}}|{{.Size}}`). The field name and its per-row semantics should be confirmed against `docker system df --help`/docs rather than assumed, since a field-name or semantic mismatch emits wrong bytes silently.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdd7c4471fa1060b4","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Observability (S2's publish-or-stay-silent rule) — `container_writable_bytes`/`container_exited_bytes`","norm_id":"n97c8832b8302b47e","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["`{{.Reclaimable}}` renders empty or a human-formatted string the parser mishandles","the Containers `.Size` includes shared/base image layers, so `container_writable_bytes` overstates true writable footprint"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_cla